libthe-seed (unreleased)

* Plugins are pinned. Every plugin that ComponentLoader, SystemLoader and
  LibraryLoader open stays loaded until the process ends, so components,
  systems, creators and scene contents stay valid and destructible after their
  loader is destroyed, in any order. Destroying a loader no longer unloads
  anything.

* Search order: locations added with PathAdd are searched first, in order, and
  the first location holding the file decides. A damaged file is reported, not
  skipped for a later copy. The file is opened by absolute path. The working
  directory is never searched unless it is added with PathAdd. This applies to
  ComponentLoader, SystemLoader, PakLoader and LibraryLoader.

* Development locations (../../<library>/src/.libs and
  ../node_modules/<org>/<library>/src/.libs) are searched after the
  configured locations instead of before them. New: SearchPathsGet(name) on
  ComponentLoader, SystemLoader and PakLoader.

* LoadError (new, installed, derives from std::runtime_error) reports every
  failure to load a plugin, resource pak or scene with a reason (InvalidName,
  NotFound, NotLoadable, EntryPointMissing, NoObject, SceneUnopenable,
  SceneNotUnderstood, SceneComponentFailed), the name, the file, every
  location searched and the platform's own text. Code that caught
  std::invalid_argument or nlohmann::json::parse_error from a loader must
  catch LoadError.

* Name rules: a plugin name is "library" or "org/library"; empty parts, "." and
  ".." parts, backslashes, ":", control characters, a leading "/" and more than
  one "/" are refused with InvalidName before any file is touched.

* JSONLoader is all or nothing: a scene that fails leaves the container
  unchanged. A missing or unreadable file is SceneUnopenable rather than a
  parse error at line 1, column 1. A scene without "entities", or an entity
  without "Handle" or "Components", is now an error (SceneNotUnderstood).

* LibraryLoader::PathsGet returns the locations added with PathAdd and never
  throws (it used to return the library files found and throw when there were
  none).

* Concurrent loads: one open per plugin file per loader, concurrent requests
  for one name share one load, and a failed load is not remembered.

* Tests: configure --enable-sanitizer=thread builds the library, the tests and
  the test plugins with ThreadSanitizer. The README examples are compiled and
  run by test_ReadmeExamples.

* ABI: the private members of every loader changed. Rebuild programs against
  the new headers. No version change; the version is set when the work is
  released.

libthe-seed 0.7.0

* MsiSigner computes the same Authenticode fingerprint as osslsigncode 2.14
  and writes signed packages that osslsigncode and an independent reader read
  back. Every operation rebuilds the package in one canonical layout: the
  signature is placed in the mini stream below the 4,096 byte cut-off and in
  ordinary sectors from it, the directory entry sits at its sorted position,
  \005MsiDigitalSignatureEx is dropped, other streams and storages keep their
  names, bytes, class identifiers, state bits and times, and the output is
  deterministic.

* EmbedSignature gains require_matching_digest (default false): when true the
  blob must hold the fingerprint of the package being written, otherwise the
  call is refused and the file is unchanged. An empty blob is refused.

* StripSignature now returns bool: true when a signature stream was removed,
  false when there was none (the file is then untouched). It does not read
  the old signature.

* CheckSignature (new) reports None, Matches, Mismatch or Unreadable. Matches
  compares fingerprints only and does not say the signature is valid.

* Packages with two entries of one name in a storage, storages nested deeper
  than 32 levels, and packages beyond the format's limits are refused with the
  file unchanged.

* Versions up to 0.6.0 produced installers that only look signed. Packages
  signed by earlier versions of the-seed are repaired when signed again;
  re-sign them from the unsigned original when you have it.

* What is and is not verified: The fingerprint and the package structure written by libthe-seed were compared with osslsigncode 2.14, with an independent reader written for the tests, and (for stream lookup by name) with Wine 10's structured-storage implementation. They were not checked with Microsoft's signtool, WinVerifyTrust, the Windows Installer service or Microsoft's own storage code, because no Windows machine is part of the test setup. Certificate trust is not checked. Installers signed by earlier versions of the-seed may be damaged; re-sign them from the unsigned original when you have it.
  The signature container that the-seed builds has no signed attributes and its cryptography is not checked by this library, so standard verifiers may reject it.

* Version 0.7.0 (was 0.6.0). The libtool library version is unchanged.

libthe-seed 0.6.0

* MachOSigner signs Mac programs in two calls, PrepareSignature and
  CompleteSignature (new). The CodeDirectory is computed over the finished
  layout, so the page fingerprints match the file. Signing an already signed
  program replaces the signature in place; StripSignature (new) removes it.
  A program without room for the signature command is refused and left
  unchanged, with the bytes needed and available; relink with extra header
  space (for example -headerpad 0x20). Big-endian and 32-bit programs are
  refused with a message that names the kind.

* ComputeCodeDirectory and EmbedSignature are removed: removed because hashing
  before the file is laid out cannot yield a valid signature; use
  PrepareSignature and CompleteSignature.

* MachOParser reads the real file layout (thin and universal, 32 and 64 bit
  universal tables); GetArchSlices has additive fields for the signature and
  for declined slices. HasEmbeddedSignature is true for a universal file only
  when every slice is signed.

* DependencyLister now lists Mach-O programs and libraries (it declined them
  in 0.5.0), reading every slice. Names with a folder separator, such as
  @rpath/ names, are listed under the recorded name.

* What is and is not verified: Page fingerprints in a signature produced by
  this library match the finished file; this is checked by an independent
  checker and by values recorded from Python's hashlib. The checker accepts
  the ad-hoc signature written by ld64.lld, a different producer. The
  structure of signed files parses with llvm-otool, llvm-objdump and
  llvm-lipo. Nobody has checked a signature produced by this library with
  the platform's own verifier (`codesign --verify`) or by running a signed
  program on a Mac. What was checked is described above. The CMS part of the
  signature is the minimal one the-seed has always produced and is not known
  to be accepted by Apple's tools. Programs signed by earlier versions of
  the-seed are malformed after re-signing and may need to be rebuilt from
  their unsigned originals.

* Version 0.6.0 (was 0.5.0). The libtool library version is unchanged.

libthe-seed 0.5.0

* DependencyLister now credits every input program with every library it
  needs, directly or through other libraries. Before, a library reached by
  several programs was credited only to the first one that reached it, so the
  result depended on the order of the inputs.

  Packaging output for existing projects can grow: more libraries are now
  attributed to the programs that need them, including libraries that were
  previously missing from every program but the first, and delay-loaded Windows
  libraries. This is the intended correction. Check bundle contents and sizes
  after upgrading.

* Delay-loaded libraries of Windows programs (the delay-load import table) are
  now listed. A malformed delay-load table is rejected like any other
  malformed PE structure.

* New field DependencyResult::libraryErrors (additive; a caller that ignores
  it sees the same keys and errors as before). A library that was found but
  cannot be read is still listed in `dependencies`, and is now reported here
  with the reason and the sorted list of inputs that need it. `errors` still
  holds only inputs named in the request.

* The lists in `dependencies` are now sorted. Libraries are keyed by the real
  file's canonical path, or by the recorded name when not found. PE library
  names match without regard to letter case; ELF names match exactly. Names
  containing a folder separator, "..", a drive prefix or a NUL are not joined
  to a search folder; they are listed under the recorded name.

* Mach-O inputs are declined: the input appears in `errors` with
  "<path>: Mach-O files are not supported for dependency listing" (a Mach-O
  library gets the same text in `libraryErrors`). This will be revisited after
  roadmap task 5. MachOParser::ListDependencies now reads weak, re-exported,
  lazy and upward references, reads every slice of a universal file and
  rejects an unterminated library name.

* Version 0.5.0 (was 0.4.1). The libtool library version is unchanged.
